ps://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested locally, it works as expected.\r\n\r\nNote that the rebase is non-trivial, as the the Tree drop indicator PR was recently merged.\r\n\r\nSome feedback:\r\n\r\n- Right-clicking a sticky item should probably *not* scroll to it, so that you can open the context menu related to the item without scrolling up. Only left-clicking a sticky item should scroll to it.\r\n\r\n- Selecting items with the arrow keys can leave the selected item invisible:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0add3ec7-7c87-43c7-ab28-ced0fe60ca6d\r\n\r\n- I'm concerned about the usable height of the Tree potentially decreasing a lot in certain scenes. This is particularly a problem on displays where vertical screen real estate is at a premium, such as 16:9 laptops, Macs with the Dock always visible (the default), and so on.\r\n\r\n  - A breadcrumbs solution similar to what VS Code features at the top of the file view might be preferable for this. It lets you show multiple node names on the same line, provided the inspector is width enough. If there isn't enough space, then we can compact the display by showing only the first letters of each node name, or possibly just show the node icon.\r\n\r\nRough mockup of what it'd look like:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"276\" height=\"240\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4159a649-a8d1-4f81-b7ca-1fe47710313b\" />\r\n\r\n  - Perhaps we should show just *one* sticky item, which would be the direct parent of the currently selected node. This would be helpful in long lists of sibling nodes, but wouldn't trade up too much vertical space. VS Code also does this with the function signature as seen in this screenshot:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"327\" height=\"94\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d80c00fa-a2de-4776-b65d-760fbff10c42\" />","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115697#pullrequestreview-4077344695","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115697","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115697#pullrequestreview-4077344695"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115697"}},"submitted_at":"2026-04-08T18:28:58Z","commit_id":"56a02831e75e4eb170093db8c208f42515b42eae"},{"id":4135196431,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc72ehcP","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?u=fc85633b469acb6e7baef4dba5171f19a2a4ff85&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"h